IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `roc-core`
IMPORT `roc12-schedule-4-types`
IMPORT `roc12-schedule-4-part-1`
IMPORT `roc12-schedule-4-part-2`
IMPORT `roc12-schedule-4-part-3`
IMPORT `roc12-schedule-4-part-4`
IMPORT `roc12-schedule-4-part-5`

-- Rules of Court 2021 (Singapore), G.N. No. S 914/2021, current version as at 5 November 2026.
-- THE FOURTH SCHEDULE (COURT FEES): ASKING FOR A FEE (part roc12, layer 1).
-- Source: a plain-text rendering made by a converter script from Singapore Statutes Online.
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here has been checked against the official text.
--
-- The seam `sch 4 the fee for this document` (S-V3) is the function any rule that says "a fee is payable" asks.
-- It answers `MAYBE NUMBER`: JUST the sum, or NOTHING when the row has no such item, no fee in that column, or states
-- its fee in words only.  A caller must never turn NOTHING into 0.

-- ===========================================================================
§ `Fourth Schedule -- the row for a Part and an item`
-- ===========================================================================

GIVEN part IS A NUMBER
      item IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE `sch 4 row`
`sch 4 the row for the part and item` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF part EQUALS 1 THEN `sch 4 part 1 the row for the item` item
        IF part EQUALS 2 THEN `sch 4 part 2 the row for the item` item
        IF part EQUALS 3 THEN `sch 4 part 3 the row for the item` item
        IF part EQUALS 4 THEN `sch 4 part 4 the row for the item` item
        IF part EQUALS 5 THEN `sch 4 part 5 the row for the item` item
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the Fourth Schedule has five Parts

-- S-V3: the fee for this document.  `item` is the row's identifier as the Part file lists it (for example "1", "7(k)(ii)", "44A", or for Part 2 "table 1 item 1").
GIVEN part IS A NUMBER
      item IS A STRING
      column IS A `sch 4 column`
      units IS A NUMBER
      base IS A NUMBER
      documents IS A NUMBER
      `the fee payable for the last application` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`sch 4 the fee for this document` MEANS
    CONSIDER `sch 4 the row for the part and item` part item
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the Fourth Schedule has no such item
    WHEN JUST row THEN
        CONSIDER `sch 4 the fee in the row for the column` row column
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the row has no fee for that column, or prints no cell of its own
        WHEN JUST fee THEN `sch 4 the amount payable under the fee` fee units base documents `the fee payable for the last application`

-- The same, for a court and a value of claim: the column is the Schedule's own (Supreme Court by value, or District Court, or Magistrate's Court).
GIVEN part IS A NUMBER
      item IS A STRING
      `the court system` IS A `Court system`
      `the court level` IS A `Court level`
      `o 25 r 2 the value of the claim` IS A NUMBER
      units IS A NUMBER
      base IS A NUMBER
      documents IS A NUMBER
      `the fee payable for the last application` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`sch 4 the fee for this document in the proceedings` MEANS
    CONSIDER `sch 4 the column for the proceedings` `the court system` `the court level` `o 25 r 2 the value of the claim`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the Schedule has no column for that court
    WHEN JUST column THEN `sch 4 the fee for this document` part item column units base documents `the fee payable for the last application`

-- The same, for a search fee, for a court and a value of claim.
GIVEN part IS A NUMBER
      item IS A STRING
      `the court system` IS A `Court system`
      `the court level` IS A `Court level`
      `o 25 r 2 the value of the claim` IS A NUMBER
      units IS A NUMBER
      base IS A NUMBER
      documents IS A NUMBER
      `the fee payable for the last application` IS A NUMBER
      `the searcher is a subscriber` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`sch 4 the fee for this document in the proceedings for a searcher` MEANS
    CONSIDER `sch 4 the column for the proceedings` `the court system` `the court level` `o 25 r 2 the value of the claim`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the Schedule has no column for that court
    WHEN JUST column THEN `sch 4 the fee for this document for a searcher` part item column units base documents `the fee payable for the last application` `the searcher is a subscriber`

-- The count is `units`.  A fee charged "for each" party, witness, day, hour, document, exhibit, attempt, address, request, book or search term comes to the
-- sum times the count (the row's own unit noun says which count); a hearing fee "after the first day" or for the "fourth day" and on counts the days the hearing lasts.
-- A count of 0 owes nothing.  The fee of one event ("on every request", "on filing") is for that one event: a caller with several events asks once for each.

-- A search fee (Part 4 item 1(b)): the searcher's status picks the sum, and `units` is the number of search terms (for each module, for each year).
GIVEN part IS A NUMBER
      item IS A STRING
      column IS A `sch 4 column`
      units IS A NUMBER
      base IS A NUMBER
      documents IS A NUMBER
      `the fee payable for the last application` IS A NUMBER
      `the searcher is a subscriber` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`sch 4 the fee for this document for a searcher` MEANS
    CONSIDER `sch 4 the row for the part and item` part item
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the Fourth Schedule has no such item
    WHEN JUST row THEN
        CONSIDER `sch 4 the fee in the row for the column` row column
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the row has no fee for that column, or prints no cell of its own
        WHEN JUST fee THEN `sch 4 the amount payable under the fee for a searcher` fee units base documents `the fee payable for the last application` `the searcher is a subscriber`

-- The yes/no twin of the seam: is the sum a person states the fee the Schedule charges for this count?
-- JUST FALSE when the Schedule prints a sum and the stated sum is not it (the Schedule's sum is fixed in its own words); NOTHING when the Schedule prints no sum (a cell in words, no such item or column).
GIVEN part IS A NUMBER
      item IS A STRING
      column IS A `sch 4 column`
      units IS A NUMBER
      base IS A NUMBER
      documents IS A NUMBER
      `the fee payable for the last application` IS A NUMBER
      `the fee stated` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 4 the stated fee is the fee charged` MEANS
    CONSIDER `sch 4 the fee for this document` part item column units base documents `the fee payable for the last application`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the Schedule prints no sum for that item, column and count, so it does not say that any stated fee is the one charged
    WHEN JUST charged THEN JUST (`the fee stated` EQUALS charged) -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): a sum other than the one the Schedule prints is not the fee

-- The same for a search fee, where the searcher's status picks the sum.
GIVEN part IS A NUMBER
      item IS A STRING
      column IS A `sch 4 column`
      units IS A NUMBER
      base IS A NUMBER
      documents IS A NUMBER
      `the fee payable for the last application` IS A NUMBER
      `the searcher is a subscriber` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the fee stated` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 4 the stated fee is the fee charged to a searcher` MEANS
    CONSIDER `sch 4 the fee for this document for a searcher` part item column units base documents `the fee payable for the last application` `the searcher is a subscriber`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the Schedule prints no sum for that item, column and count
    WHEN JUST charged THEN JUST (`the fee stated` EQUALS charged) -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): a sum other than the one the Schedule prints is not the fee

-- Items 13 and 14: an order to attend court and/or to produce documents is charged "for each witness", at item 14's rate when it is urgent
-- (issued less than 3 days before the trial: item 14's note) and at item 13's rate when it is "other than an urgent order".
-- src:8026 | On sealing an order to attend court and/or to produce documents, other than an urgent order to attend court and/or to produce documents, for each witness
-- src:8027 | $50
-- src:8028 | $100
-- src:8029 | $10
-- src:8030 | $10
-- src:8031 | Order to attend court and/or to produce documents
-- src:8032 | 14.
-- src:8033 | On sealing an urgent order to attend court and/or to produce documents, for each witness
-- src:8034 | Note : An urgent order to attend court and/or to produce documents is an order that is issued less than 3 days before the trial of an action
-- src:8035 | $100
-- src:8036 | $200
-- src:8037 | $20
-- src:8038 | $20
@ref Sch 4 part 1 items 13 and 14 (src:8026-8038)
GIVEN column IS A `sch 4 column`
      witnesses IS A NUMBER
      `the date the order is issued` IS A DATE
      `the first day of the trial of the action` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`sch 4 part 1 items 13 and 14 the fee for an order to attend court and or to produce documents` MEANS
    CONSIDER `sch 4 part 1 item 14 the order is an urgent order` `the date the order is issued` `the first day of the trial of the action`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the note defines an urgent order and says nothing when its dates are not given
    WHEN JUST urgent THEN
        IF urgent
        THEN `sch 4 the fee for this document` 1 "14" column witnesses 0 1 0
        ELSE `sch 4 the fee for this document` 1 "13" column witnesses 0 1 0

-- Item 46: the row prints one set of cells for the five things listed under it; (b) adds "for each opening".
-- This function charges item 46's cell for each opening of the account, a transcript of an account being charged "for each opening".
-- src:8364 | ( b )
-- src:8365 | on a transcript of an account on the same for each opening, including the request of it
@ref Sch 4 part 1 item 46(b) (src:8364-8365)
GIVEN column IS A `sch 4 column`
      openings IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`sch 4 part 1 item 46(b) the fee for a transcript of an account` MEANS
    CONSIDER `sch 4 the fee for this document` 1 "46" column 1 0 1 0
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): item 46 prints no fee in that column
    WHEN JUST feeForOne THEN JUST (feeForOne TIMES openings)

-- The sum of two amounts that may be missing: NOTHING if either is.
GIVEN first IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      second IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`sch 4 the sum of two amounts` MEANS
    CONSIDER first
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): one of the amounts is not stated
    WHEN JUST x THEN
        CONSIDER second
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): one of the amounts is not stated
        WHEN JUST y THEN JUST (x PLUS y)

-- Part 2 Table 3 (hearing before a Judge sitting in the General Division): the fee for the whole hearing, from its first day.
-- The Table charges nothing for days 1 to 3 (it has no row for them; fork F-S4-A5), $a for the whole or part of the fourth day, $b for the fifth,
-- $c for each day of the sixth to tenth days and $d for each day after the tenth: a hearing of 3 days or fewer owes 0.
GIVEN column IS A `sch 4 column`
      days IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`sch 4 part 2 table 3 the hearing fee for a hearing of this many days` MEANS
    `sch 4 the sum of two amounts`
        (`sch 4 the sum of two amounts`
            (`sch 4 the fee for this document` 2 "table 3 item 1" column days 0 1 0)
            (`sch 4 the fee for this document` 2 "table 3 item 2" column days 0 1 0))
        (`sch 4 the sum of two amounts`
            (`sch 4 the fee for this document` 2 "table 3 item 3" column days 0 1 0)
            (`sch 4 the fee for this document` 2 "table 3 item 4" column days 0 1 0))

-- Part 2 Table 4 (hearing before the Registrar in the General Division for assessment of damages and the like): the fee for the whole hearing.
-- The days counted include the days taken for the determination of liability before a Judge (item 1's words); a hearing of 3 days or fewer owes 0.
GIVEN days IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`sch 4 part 2 table 4 the hearing fee for a hearing of this many days` MEANS
    `sch 4 the sum of two amounts`
        (`sch 4 the fee for this document` 2 "table 4 item 1" `sch 4 column General Division` days 0 1 0)
        (`sch 4 the fee for this document` 2 "table 4 item 2" `sch 4 column General Division` days 0 1 0)

-- Table 3 for a court and a value of claim: the Supreme Court column the value picks.
GIVEN `the court system` IS A `Court system`
      `the court level` IS A `Court level`
      `o 25 r 2 the value of the claim` IS A NUMBER
      days IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`sch 4 part 2 table 3 the hearing fee in the proceedings for a hearing of this many days` MEANS
    CONSIDER `sch 4 the column for the proceedings` `the court system` `the court level` `o 25 r 2 the value of the claim`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the Schedule has no column for that court
    WHEN JUST column THEN `sch 4 part 2 table 3 the hearing fee for a hearing of this many days` column days

-- The fee for one day of a Table 3 hearing: the whole fee for a hearing that lasts to that day, less the whole fee for one day fewer.
-- It is 0 for the first three days, $a on the fourth, $b on the fifth, $c on each of the sixth to tenth and $d on each day after.  A day before the first has no fee to state (NOTHING).
GIVEN `the court system` IS A `Court system`
      `the court level` IS A `Court level`
      `o 25 r 2 the value of the claim` IS A NUMBER
      day IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`sch 4 part 2 table 3 the fee for one day of the hearing in the proceedings` MEANS
    IF day LESS THAN 1
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): there is no such day of a hearing
    ELSE CONSIDER `sch 4 part 2 table 3 the hearing fee in the proceedings for a hearing of this many days` `the court system` `the court level` `o 25 r 2 the value of the claim` day
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the Schedule has no column for that court
         WHEN JUST throughThisDay THEN
             CONSIDER `sch 4 part 2 table 3 the hearing fee in the proceedings for a hearing of this many days` `the court system` `the court level` `o 25 r 2 the value of the claim` (day MINUS 1)
             WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the Schedule has no column for that court
             WHEN JUST throughTheDayBefore THEN JUST (throughThisDay MINUS throughTheDayBefore)

-- The same for Table 4: 0 for the first three days, $1,000 on the fourth and on each day after.
GIVEN day IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`sch 4 part 2 table 4 the fee for one day of the hearing` MEANS
    IF day LESS THAN 1
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): there is no such day of a hearing
    ELSE CONSIDER `sch 4 part 2 table 4 the hearing fee for a hearing of this many days` day
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the Table states no sum
         WHEN JUST throughThisDay THEN
             CONSIDER `sch 4 part 2 table 4 the hearing fee for a hearing of this many days` (day MINUS 1)
             WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the Table states no sum
             WHEN JUST throughTheDayBefore THEN JUST (throughThisDay MINUS throughTheDayBefore)

